# `yo build` itself must print no effect-unwind diagnostic. The build runner
# makes its read_dir / read_bytes / stamp-write tasks fallible on purpose: a
# swallow handler unwinds the task and the spawner reads `.None` at the
# awaited handle. v0.2.40 reported every one of those aborts as unhandled
# (18 lines on a plain build) — issues/fixed/an-awaited-task-abort-is-reported-as-unhandled.md.
# The program aborts nothing, so any unwind line here is the compiler's own.
#
# This case measures the SELF-HOSTED binary's own runtime, which follows the
# SEED's codegen, so it could only be added once the seed carried the fix
# (v0.2.41). The pattern keeps both wordings of the diagnostic plus the
# build's header line, so the case is never vacuous.
stdout_keep_match=(unhandled effect unwind[a-z ]*|Building [a-z]+)
timeout=300
